+# MUWEB R90 FIX98 — Equipment Raw-BMD/Reattach
+
+Parent: FIX97 Character Visibility Parse Owner.
+
+## Closed
+- Split BMD contracts in MUAssetLoader: `loadBMDRaw()` owns parser structures (`meshes[].triangles/vertices/normals`); `loadBMD()` owns adapted Three.js render-data.
+- `buildEquipmentAttach()` now loads weapons, body replacements, wings and attachable helpers through `loadBMDRaw()`.
+- Base class Helm/Armor/Pant/Glove/Boot use the same raw cache instead of reparsing independently.
+- Adapted render BMD is derived from the authority-scoped raw parse, preserving one parser owner and avoiding the FIX88 type-confusion regression.
+
+## Symptoms fixed
+- `m.triangles is not iterable` during F3:13 staged reattach.
+- Follow-on `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'map')` when accessory/body candidate was built from incomplete adapted data.
+- Equipped items visible in inventory but absent on character due to failed reattach.
+
+## Not claimed
+Custom item-specific missing assets/model mappings remain fail-closed if the physical BMD itself is absent or invalid.
